Body:
Try setting the temperature to 1.0 in `opencode.json`:

```json
	"provider": {
		"zai-coding-plan": {
			"models": {
				"glm-5": {
					"options": {
						"temperature": 1.0
					}
				},
				"glm-5.1": {
					"options": {
						"temperature": 1.0
					}
				}
			}
		}
	}
```
The [transform.ts](https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/blob/dev/packages/opencode/src/provider/transform.ts#L330) file doesn't have this config yet. With temperature 1.0, GLM-5 and GLM-5.1 feel more stable to me.

> Wait why is ur provider called "foundary"
> 
> If it was called "azure" I think it'd work but it's not?

It does work after I change the namespace from `foundary` to `azure` (tested on opencode v1.3.13)

```
  "provider": {
    "azure": {
      "npm": "@ai-sdk/azure",
      "options": {
        "baseURL": "https://custom-domain/openai",
        "apiKey": "xxxxxxxx",
        "apiVersion": "2025-04-01-preview",
        "useDeploymentBasedUrls": true,
        "useCompletionUrls": true
      },
      "models": {
        "gpt-5.4": {
          "name": "GPT-5.4"
        }
      }
    }
  }
```

I thought this is just a display name tag in TUI model select, separating custom provider with default provider, didn't know it have actual mapping functionality

Does this mean `provider[key]` and  `provider[key].npm` always need to pair up correctly?
